codex
The full repository gates are green, but the durability audit found a remaining crash-consistency defect before the first swap: staged file/directory creation is synced internally, yet its parent directory is never synced before the journal advances to `prepared`. A power loss can therefore retain the durable journal while losing the staging namespace entry, contradicting the package’s own “fully durable staging” phase invariant and deterministic restart commit. I’m recording this as ordinary implementation rework, not a stop-the-line blocker.
